1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,847
In SpaceX's third-quarter revenue,

2
00:00:01,867 --> 00:00:04,141
rocket launches were just 12%

3
00:00:04,161 --> 00:00:06,974
So where did the rest come from?

4
00:00:06,994 --> 00:00:09,657
Rockets $1.77B, Starlink $5.25B

5
00:00:09,677 --> 00:00:13,721
And number one was AI, at $7.56 billion

6
00:00:13,741 --> 00:00:17,371
The secret is surprisingly simple. It rented out AI computers

7
00:00:17,391 --> 00:00:21,816
The rocket company's side shop turned out to be a giant computer rental business

8
00:00:21,836 --> 00:00:25,668
Anthropic, the maker of Claude, pays $1.25 billion a month,

9
00:00:25,688 --> 00:00:27,754
and Google pays $920 million

10
00:00:27,774 --> 00:00:34,025
Together that's about $26 billion a year, more than SpaceX's entire revenue last year

11
00:00:34,045 --> 00:00:37,556
But either side can end the Anthropic deal with 90 days' notice,

12
00:00:37,576 --> 00:00:40,957
and once AI chips are plentiful, rents could fall

13
00:00:40,977 --> 00:00:44,573
A space company now earns more from data centers on the ground

14
00:00:44,593 --> 00:00:47,718
